#| Off-site archive of each EXTRA instance's claims (jg-cluster-template#202),
   the per-instance twin of jg-base's base-`im` CronJob
   (kubernetes/apps/base/claudecode/claude-code/im/enabled/state-archive.yaml).

   Why it is rendered here and not shipped from jg-base: a pod spec must NAME
   the claims it mounts, and an extra's claims are `<instance>-claude-config`
   / `<instance>-claude-workspace` -- names that exist only in this cluster's
   `claude_instances`.

   What is NOT here, on purpose: the script, the credentials, the identity.
   This CronJob runs jg-base's ConfigMap `claudecode-archive-script`, reads its
   Secret `claudecode-archive-config` and runs as its SA `claudecode-archive`
   (all in jg-base `claude-code/app/`, applied on every cluster since
   ferry133/jg-base#178). One copy of the session cap and the exclusion list,
   still under the jg-base guards that execute them; one copy of the BACKUP_*
   values. Re-typing either here would put a second copy outside every guard.
   ARCHIVE_INSTANCE / ARCHIVE_MEMBERS are that script's only per-caller knobs.

   An `im/disabled` cluster (claudecode_auth0: false) is the one this matters
   most for: its only terminal is an extra, and `kubectl exec` (monitoring's
   offsite-backup) cannot reach an extra at 0 replicas -- which is how extras
   sit by default.

   The YAML comment below is outside the loop on purpose (jgct#229): with no
   instances the loop renders nothing, makejinja does not write an empty
   render, and kustomization.yaml would list a file that does not exist.
   kustomize accepts a comment-only resource file. #|
# Archive CronJobs for the extra instances in claude_instances; none if it is empty.
#% for instance in claude_instances %#
---
apiVersion: batch/v1
kind: CronJob
metadata:
  name: #{instance}#-state-backup
  namespace: claudecode
  labels:
    # jg-base's daily-check selects backup jobs by this label OR a `-backup`
    # name; carry both, as the base CronJob does (jg-base#85).
    app.kubernetes.io/component: backup
spec:
  # Half an hour after the base im archive (0 19), itself an hour after
  # offsite-backup (0 18): no two uploads share a window on a slow link.
  schedule: "30 19 * * *"
  timeZone: "Etc/UTC"
  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid
  startingDeadlineSeconds: 3600
  successfulJobsHistoryLimit: 3
  failedJobsHistoryLimit: 3
  jobTemplate:
    spec:
      backoffLimit: 1
      # Coupled to failedJobsHistoryLimit: retaining 3 daily runs needs 3 days
      # (jg-base#143 -- the stricter knob wins silently).
      ttlSecondsAfterFinished: 259200
      activeDeadlineSeconds: 3600
      template:
        spec:
          restartPolicy: Never
          serviceAccountName: claudecode-archive
          securityContext:
            # The claims are written by the instance as uid 0 (the NAS/NFS
            # convention), so they are read as uid 0.
            runAsNonRoot: false
            seccompProfile:
              type: RuntimeDefault
          # ⚠️ PREFERRED, not required -- copied with its reason from the base
          # CronJob. RWO is a NODE-scoped lock, so co-locating with a running
          # instance avoids a multi-attach stall. But `required` matches
          # EXISTING pods, and an extra at 0 replicas (the default, and the
          # case this Job exists for) has none: the archive would sit Pending
          # forever, reading exactly like an archive with nothing to do. With
          # the instance at 0 the volume is attached nowhere and any node can
          # take it. What preferred does NOT guarantee on a multi-node cluster
          # with the instance RUNNING is co-location; that case is unmeasured
          # here as it is for the base im.
          affinity:
            podAffinity:
              preferredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:
                - weight: 100
                  podAffinityTerm:
                    labelSelector:
                      matchLabels:
                        app.kubernetes.io/name: #{instance}#
                    topologyKey: kubernetes.io/hostname
          containers:
            - name: archive
              # ⚠️ The same pre-baked ops image as jg-base's base archive, pinned
              # by hand in TWO repos: jg-base bumps its own copy, nothing bumps
              # this one. A stale pin still runs (the script is in the ConfigMap,
              # not the image); it only needs age, aws-cli, tar and gzip.
              image: ghcr.io/ferry133/claude-code:ops-b8fe918@sha256:c1130a0ff0ca5d344c5bc34831e63bf83cb09755365d343d0922404fd5aa69be
              command:
                - /bin/bash
                - /scripts/archive.sh
              env:
                - name: ARCHIVE_INSTANCE
                  value: "#{instance}#"
                #| Follows the SAME condition that adds the workspace claim to the
                   HelmRelease (helmrelease.yaml.j2): naming a member the Job
                   does not mount is FATAL in archive.sh, and mounting a claim
                   the release did not create leaves the pod Pending forever. #|
                - name: ARCHIVE_MEMBERS
                  value: "#{ 'config workspace' if claudecode_workspace else 'config' }#"
              envFrom:
                - secretRef:
                    name: claudecode-archive-config
              volumeMounts:
                - name: scripts
                  mountPath: /scripts
                # Read-only: this Job copies state out; a bug that wrote into
                # the live claim would be a bug in the thing meant to protect it.
                - name: claude-config
                  mountPath: /state/config
                  readOnly: true
#% if claudecode_workspace %#
                - name: claude-workspace
                  mountPath: /state/workspace
                  readOnly: true
#% endif %#
          volumes:
            - name: scripts
              configMap:
                name: claudecode-archive-script
                defaultMode: 0555
            # app-template names a claim `<release>-<persistence key>`.
            - name: claude-config
              persistentVolumeClaim:
                claimName: #{instance}#-claude-config
                readOnly: true
#% if claudecode_workspace %#
            - name: claude-workspace
              persistentVolumeClaim:
                claimName: #{instance}#-claude-workspace
                readOnly: true
#% endif %#
#% endfor %#
